      "admissible": false,
      "reason": "Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.4308813 describes virtual STL models made for 3D printing, including smoothed versions. Peterman, Ritterbush, Hoffmann and others built the ammonoid septa by wrapping a suture and smoothing toward a minimum-curvature surface, and built the nautiloid septum as a hemisphere (Scientific Reports 2021, s41598-021-87379-5, methods). A surface constructed to be minimal cannot test the claim.",
