        "license": {
          "id": "cc-by-3.0"
        },
        "description_excerpt": "<p>Virtual models (in STL format) of ectocochleate (externally-shelled) cephalopod chambers (camerae) and divider walls (septa). These models were 3D printed to measure their retention of liquid by surface tension. This zip folder contains models of two types: 1) single septa for different species confined in a cylindrical shell, and 2) entire camerae of two species. The latter models have several iterations of smoothed versions for comparison.&nbsp;</p>",
